        outsideEvidence: "A strong essay could add outside evidence such as the specific contrast between the Knights of Labor's and AFL's differing strategies (Section 6.3) as a further illustration of internal debate within the labor movement, or the Chinese Exclusion Act (Section 6.4) as an example of a different kind of organized political response (nativist) achieving more immediate legislative success than either labor or Populist organizing did during this same period.",
        sourcingModel: "Example sourcing sentence (Document 2): Since this injunction was issued by a federal court whose institutional role was to rule on the legality of the strikers' actions specifically under interstate commerce law, its characterization of the strike as an 'illegal restraint on commerce' reflects a particular legal framework and institutional interest in orderly commerce — not a neutral assessment of the strikers' underlying grievances, which Document 1's wage data suggests were substantively real."
